{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-2","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-2","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":392,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#lem:dc-ch7-3-2","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-3-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-3-4]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-smooth]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#prop:dc-ch5-3-5]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch7-3-2","line":668,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[no conjugate points when $K\\le 0$]\n\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch7-3-2}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch5-2-1, def:dc-ch5-3-1, def:dc-ch5-3-4, lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate, lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-smooth}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:3.2}\nLet $M$ be a complete Riemannian manifold with $K(p,\\sigma)\\le 0$ for all $p\\in M$\n  and for all $\\sigma\\subset T_pM$. Then for all $p\\in M$ the conjugate locus\n  $C(p)=\\varnothing$; in particular the exponential map $\\exp_p:T_pM\\to M$ is a local\n  diffeomorphism.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate, prop:dc-ch5-3-5}\n\\sketch Apply \\cref{lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate} to every geodesic from $p$. The absence of conjugate points makes the differential of $\\exp_p$ an isomorphism at every vector; the inverse function theorem then gives a smooth local diffeomorphism.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[no conjugate points when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K\\le 0$\">$K\\le 0$</span>] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d332d32\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23def%3Adc-ch5-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch5-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23def%3Adc-ch5-3-1\">↗ def:dc-ch5-3-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23def%3Adc-ch5-3-4\">↗ def:dc-ch5-3-4</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-expmap-smooth\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-smooth</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:3.2</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a complete Riemannian manifold with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K(p,\\sigma )\\le 0$\">$K(p,\\sigma )\\le 0$</span> for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> and for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma \\subset T_pM$\">$\\sigma \\subset T_pM$</span>. Then for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> the conjugate locus <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C(p)=\\varnothing $\">$C(p)=\\varnothing $</span>; in particular the exponential map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p:T_pM\\to M$\">$\\exp _p:T_pM\\to M$</span> is a local diffeomorphism.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23prop%3Adc-ch5-3-5\">↗ prop:dc-ch5-3-5</a> \\sketch Apply <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d332d322d6e6f2d636f6e6a7567617465\">section 2</a> to every geodesic from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>. The absence of conjugate points makes the differential of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> an isomorphism at every vector; the inverse function theorem then gives a smooth local diffeomorphism. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-3-length-expansion","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch5-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Do