y \\cref{lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate} to every geodesic from $p$. The absence of conjugate points makes the differential of $\\exp_p$ an isomorphism at every vector; the inverse function theorem then gives a smooth local diffeomorphism.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-2-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-3-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-3-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-3-4","title":"def:dc-ch5-3-4","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-2-no-conjugate","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-smooth","title":"lem:dc-ch7-3-expmap-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#prop:dc-ch5-3-5","title":"prop:dc-ch5-3-5","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}